  "subject": "The selected process change should have its intended observable effect specified in advance.",
  "verdict": "SATISFIED",
  "unresolved_conditions": [],
  "rationale": "The rule has a determinate trigger—selection of a process change for the trial—and a clear prospective response: specify its intended observable effect before the trial. This is internally coherent at the stated scope. An effect size or success threshold is not necessary to make this specification requirement determinate. The judgment does not establish compliance or effectiveness.",
